cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Clinical Fidelity Belt: a quantitative fidelity gate for patient-facing radiology reports"
abstract: >-
  A four-layer quantitative gate interposed between an AI humanisation service
  and patient delivery of radiology reports. It measures readability, clinical
  coverage, entity recall and factual fidelity, and decides by majority vote
  whether a humanised report is faithful enough to be given to a patient. The
  central contribution is the operational distinction between appropriate
  simplification and severity attenuation, and the demonstration that lexical
  methods cannot draw it while an LLM-as-a-judge with explicit grounding can.
